// EXPECT: E0244 — a bare `.` member with no context (ADR-0046 §3)
// `:=` infers from the initialiser, so there is no enum to resolve `RED` in. Deliberately not
// "unresolved name `RED`", which would send the reader looking for a declaration that was never
// meant to exist — and deliberately not resolved by searching every enum in scope, because that
// answer would change the day an unrelated type grew a `RED`.
Colour :: enum {
    RED;
    GREEN;
}

main :: () {
    c := .RED;
}
